Dear Alex,

=20

Thank you for your email.

I have been working on a statement in support of the following:

=20
Mr. Zahmoul=E2=80=99s role is significant within Rakishev=E2=80=99s inner circle and he=
 is very important to Rakishev.
There is unequivocal evidence that Rakishev is involved in our divorce proc=
eedings and is providing material assistance to Mr. Zahmoul with =E2=80=9CReputati=
on Laundering=E2=80=9D.
M. MacDonald J.=E2=80=99s draft judgement is completely disconnected from the evi=
dence filed, the 6,000 page- court bundle, the case summaries, the submissio=
ns, the cross examinations, the transcripts,  and the audio recordings of th=
e two-week trial.
Most notably, Mr. Zahmoul has been cleansed of everything.
=20

As stated in The Atlantic Council report of January 2023:

=20

=E2=80=9CWhen perpetrators acquire a new =E2=80=98clean=E2=80=99 image, their money-launderin=
g practices become invisible, but the individuals themselves become influent=
ial voices in Western democracies. As government has failed to address this =
problem, British professional services provision to kleptocracies is undermi=
ning the fairness and efficiency of the legal system=E2=80=9D.

=20

The allegations of money laundering are the subject of a criminal investiga=
tion by IRS CI.

It was mentioned in the court bundle, in the conduct statement, in during m=
y cross examination.=20

The judgement has been sanitized and the primary beneficiary is Rakishev.

=20

I understand that you cannot do anything because the judiciary is independe=
nt. What is also clear is that the Rakishev=E2=80=99s transnational reach is chill=
ing.

=20

The net result of what happened is that Mr. Zahmoul=E2=80=99s record remains pris=
tine, and he can continue to represent Rakishev=E2=80=99s interests in the US and =
the UK. This was the objective, and it seems that Rakishev does not have the=
 constraints that we have.

=20

The strongest aspect of my position is that it is independently verifiable.=
 A simple comparison of the draft judgement vs the court bundle and trial tr=
anscripts will demonstrate unequivocally that the two are not consistent, no=
r do they present the same narrative. Reading the draft judgement feels like=
 it is about an entirely different case.

They are divergent in tone and in content. This is an independent exercise =
with no input from me. Mr. Zahmoul=E2=80=99s cross examination confirms on the rec=
ord several millions of non-disclosures by himself. The position on all his =
wrongdoings (and there are many) is completely reversed in the judgement. He=
 has been absolved of everything.

=20

Comparing the draft judgement to the evidence filed and the transcripts (or=
 attendance notes) is all that it takes. It is simple and straightforward.

=20

If my allegations are correct, the implications are far reaching.

=20

I do not have any legal representation due to lack of funds. My barrister s=
ays he fulfilled his duty to the court, but he cannot represent me.

=20

I do not any financial resources for our living expenses and Mr. Zahmoul fa=
iled to make the monthly maintenance payments in April.=20

=20

I wrote to the judge regarding the maintenance payment, the need for legal =
counsel, and the incident involving Lila Mae. I have not heard from him.

=20

In summary, I don=E2=80=99t have money for groceries, I don=E2=80=99t have legal repres=
entation, and I don=E2=80=99t know how to appeal the judgement.

=20

The judgment will be handed down on the 18th and the beneficiary of this sa=
nitized version is Rakishev, who will continue to supply armed vehicles to K=
adyrov=E2=80=99s troops in Ukraine. Mr Zahmoul will continue to invest the oligarc=
hs=E2=80=99 money and avoid the sanctions.

=20

The cruelest part of the judgment is that after four years of battle, it re=
instates Mr. Zahmoul=E2=80=99s dominion over me and over the children, it forces m=
e to communicate with him which is something the court knows I cannot do bec=
ause of the documented abuse, and it denies my daughter=E2=80=99 Special Needs.

=20

I am sorry that there is nothing you can do. Rakeshev should be sanctioned =
but instead, he is laundering Mr. Zahmoul=E2=80=99s reputation, and will benefit p=
ersonally from this judgement.=20

=20

I am facing limited options, and I am not prepared to accept the outcome im=
posed by Rakishev and Mr. Zahmoul.=20

=20

I never intended to pursue the criminal matters in the UK, only to report t=
he ML and certain transactions to the FCA. The main point is that they have =
been entirely =E2=80=9Claundered=E2=80=9D. =20

=20

I am sincerely grateful for your support.=20

=20

Chatham House- UK=E2=80=99s kleptocracy problem,  December 2021.

=E2=80=9CKleptocracy is the extension of political and economic power into all re=
alms of life. A sign of its strength is its transnational reach. Kleptocracy=
 thrives when it can extend the corruption of institutions beyond national b=
oundaries, overcome law and regulation, and weaken support for human rights =
and constitutional democracy. As these are self-evidently damaging outcomes,=
